Package: DielectricWaterR
Title: Auditing and Exploring Dielectric Measurements of Water
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(person('Muhammad Zahir', 'Khan', email = 'zahirstat007@gmail.com',
        role = c('aut', 'cre')), person('Luqman', 'Abidoye', email =
        'kluqman2002@gmail.com', role = 'aut'))
Description: Imports, audits, compares and visualises dielectric measurements
        of water under fuel contamination and ageing. Provides descriptive
        summaries, frequency-response comparisons, confidence intervals based
        on physical-unit means, and training and testing splits that keep
        observations from the same experimental unit together.
        Experimental-unit safeguards address pseudoreplication concerns
        discussed by Hurlbert (1984) <doi:10.2307/1942661>. Grouped splitting
        is consistent with the structured-data validation principles discussed
        by Roberts et al. (2017) <doi:10.1111/ecog.02881>. Student t
        confidence intervals use the standard mean-interval formula described
        in the NIST/SEMATECH e-Handbook of Statistical Methods
        <https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/eda/section3/eda352.htm>.
        Experimental-unit identifiers are supplied by the user and are not
        inferred from material labels. This research prototype does not
        provide validated contaminant prediction or causal inference.
